<h2>

The Fastest Climber Is Usually The Best Thrower

</h2>

<p>

Before climbers reach the canopy,
they must first place their line.

The throwline is often the difference
between a quick climb and a frustrating day.

</p>

<p>

This course teaches students how to
accurately place throwballs,
isolate limbs,
select proper anchor points,
and consistently access trees
using professional arborist methods.

</p>

